cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ConnInfPy: A Unified Python Framework for Statistical Inference on Brain Connectivity Networks"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Knyazeva
    given-names: Irina
    email: knyazeva@ihb.spb.ru
    affiliation: "N.P. Bechtereva Institute of the Human Brain, Russian Academy of Sciences"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
version: "2.0.0rc1"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/IHB-IBR-department/ConnInfPy"
url: "https://ihb-ibr-department.github.io/ConnInfPy/"
abstract: "Unified Python framework for permutation-based statistical inference on brain connectivity networks (fMRI): network-based statistics (NBS, TFNBS, cNBS, NI-TFNBS, FBC-TFNBS), edge-wise GLM with Freedman-Lane permutation, multi-site ComBat harmonization and Brainnetome-based anatomical description of the results."
keywords:
  - neuroimaging
  - connectivity
  - fmri
  - network-based-statistics
  - tfnbs
  - glm
  - permutation-testing
  - fwer
  - false-discovery-rate
  - combat
